1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,165
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:03,215 --> 00:00:05,904
Robotics 101, video 7.

3
00:00:05,954 --> 00:00:09,640
Wiring the electronics safely.

4
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:14,769
Before you touch a single wire, switch the battery off.

5
00:00:14,819 --> 00:00:19,430
Ask an adult to check your wiring before you turn the power on.

6
00:00:20,750 --> 00:00:23,040
Here are the pins we use.

7
00:00:23,090 --> 00:00:28,657
The left sensor goes to pin 2 and the right sensor to pin 3.

8
00:00:28,707 --> 00:00:33,712
The motor driver uses pins 5 and 6 for speed, and pins

9
00:00:33,762 --> 00:00:36,520
8, 9, 10 and 11 for direction.

10
00:00:37,850 --> 00:00:40,587
Each sensor has three pins.

11
00:00:40,637 --> 00:00:46,058
VCC goes to 5 volts, GND goes to ground, and OUT goes

12
00:00:46,108 --> 00:00:50,600
to its Arduino pin: left to D2, right to D3.

13
00:00:51,950 --> 00:00:54,442
Now the motor driver.

14
00:00:54,492 --> 00:00:57,348
ENA to D5 and ENB to D6.

15
00:00:57,398 --> 00:01:03,159
IN1 to D8, IN2 to D9, IN3 to D10 and IN4 to D11.

16
00:01:03,209 --> 00:01:10,180
Motor A is the left motor, and motor B is the right motor.

17
00:01:11,550 --> 00:01:16,363
The battery goes to the motor driver through the switch: red to

18
00:01:16,413 --> 00:01:18,370
12 volts, black to ground.

19
00:01:18,420 --> 00:01:22,460
Then connect the driver ground to the Arduino ground.

20
00:01:22,510 --> 00:01:26,860
All grounds must be joined, or the signals will not work.

21
00:01:28,250 --> 00:01:32,258
Now ask an adult to check four things: the battery wires are

22
00:01:32,308 --> 00:01:36,856
the right way round, no bare wires touch, every ground is connected,

23
00:01:36,906 --> 00:01:40,170
and the switch stays off until the check is done.

24
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:43,475
Let us recap.

25
00:01:43,525 --> 00:01:47,126
Sensors: OUT to D2 and D3.

26
00:01:47,176 --> 00:01:53,024
Driver: ENA D5, ENB D6, IN1–IN4 on D8–D11.

27
00:01:53,074 --> 00:01:57,376
All grounds connected together.

28
00:01:57,426 --> 00:02:02,010
Next: Your first Arduino program.
